<crash-analysis>
The crash is caused by a null pointer dereference in `glslang::TInputScanner::getSourceLoc`. This function is called through a chain of functions starting from `glslang::TPpContext::tStringInput::scan`. The `scan` function calls `pp->parseContext.getCurrentLoc()`, which in turn calls `currentScanner->getSourceLoc()`. The `currentScanner` member of the `HlslParseContext` (`parseContext`) is null, leading to the crash.

The `currentScanner` is never initialized in the fuzz driver. The `HlslParseContext` is created, but its `currentScanner` member is left as a null pointer. The `TPpContext` is then initialized with this `parseContext`, and when it tries to get the source location, it dereferences the null pointer.

To fix this, the `currentScanner` of the `parseContext` needs to be set. A `TInputScanner` is created in the fuzzer, and this should be set as the `currentScanner` for the `parseContext`. The `TParseVersions` class, which `HlslParseContext` inherits from, has a public member `currentScanner`. So, the fix is to add the following line to the fuzzer after `inputScanner` is created:

```cpp
parseContext.currentScanner = inputScanner;
```
This will ensure that the `currentScanner` is valid when `getCurrentLoc` is called.
</crash-analysis>

